{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428062-tremere-path-of-flames-for-v5","id":1428062,"title":"Tremere Path of Flames for V5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-11T00:04:20-08:00","id":1428062,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Tremere Path of Flames for V5","content":"Hello everybody! &lt;3<br /> <br /> I've been working on a modification/adaptation for the <b>Path of Flames</b> for a while now and this is it! I tried to adapt the concept to V5 but also make it a more fleshed out discipline of its own.<br /> <br /> <br /> Quick summary:<br /> <br /> - Completely reworked and fully adapted discipline for V5.<br /> <br /> - Two new mechanics: <b>Mastery</b> and <b>Ignite</b>.<br /> While Ignite is more of an extra and not an integral part of the discipline, Mastery is very much so. I created the Mastery-System in order to balance the quite potent powers of the discipline, giving it a unique character and playstyle. It is a high risk - high reward playstyle, that maybe saves your coterie in the last moment - or dooms it for good. Either way, it's going to be flashy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> - 14 new powers<br /> <br /> - 6 new rituals<br /> <br /> <br /> One last thing: I'd really appriciate it, if you shared with me your experience playing it. I see this as an ongoing project and would really like to keep working on it. It would especially interest me, how the Mastery-System worked for you and what your experience using it was. This is version 1.0 and it will need some balancing down the way. You can find the contact information in the preface of the document.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks a lot and have fun playing with the Path of Flames, if you decide to do so :&gt;<br /> <br /> <br /> Comboi &lt;3<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Download:</b></span> <a href=\"https://workupload.com/file/qEDtagPpeQX\" target=\"_blank\">https://workupload.com/file/qEDtagPpeQX</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26583-comboi","name":"Comboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26583_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T03:46:44-08:00","id":1428073,"title":"","content":"Thats cool! Gonna have a look","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T04:16:28-08:00","id":1428077,"title":"","content":"That is a large amount of work you have put in and it looks good. Thanks. I might give it a try.<br /> <br /> I am very unhappy with the official V5 Fire Ritual. I don\u00b4t understand why they designed it this way. The person you are most likely to kill seems to be yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T13:31:04-08:00","id":1428120,"title":"","content":"Looks interesting, I will test it tomorrow with one of my players as she will do a Memorium to learn about ancient stuff and that character she gets to play during this will use these powers and rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T03:38:47-08:00","id":1428252,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses guys! &lt;3 <br /> <br /> Hope you're having fun with it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26583-comboi","name":"Comboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26583_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T09:07:57-08:00","id":1428280,"title":"","content":"First impression by my players. 2/4 players have reported in this far. <br /> <br /> * Good spread of powers and not just &quot;Throw bigger fireballs the more dots you have&quot;.<br /> * Interesting that you could &quot;scry&quot; with the path. very useful<br /> * The Mstery roll slowed down the game a little, not that much. But one extra roll - sometimes every round - was a little minus.<br /> * Nice thing with &quot;need level 3 in main path before advancing this to level 4&quot;<br /> * Prometheus Presence had a little too long range.<br /> * Rituals should be able to be used by standard rolls<br /> * They want you to Path of Weather Control and Movement of the Mind as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T11:51:44-08:00","id":1428289,"title":"","content":"More thoughts were just sent to me by the last 2 players:<br /> <br /> * Promethus' Insight says that &quot;the caster is also more aware of fires and a bit more resistant to falling into R\u00f6tschreck&quot; But this is not supported in the powers description.<br /> * Hephaestus' arrows has too long range.<br /> * Aodh's volley has too long range<br /> * Too many prerequisites - You have to choose from start to go either fireball lobbiing way or seer way. No other discipline has so many prereqs.<br /> * Asie from this a great initiative and a very good try to make an old path int something new.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T23:42:23-08:00","id":1428324,"title":"","content":"Thanks Ethryo and your players for the critique! Every point is noted and added to the other responses <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> A few responses and questions to your players points:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Mstery roll slowed down the game a little, not that much. But one extra roll - sometimes every round - was a little minus. </div> </div> </div>That the system slows down the game is an interesting point and is noted. A question I have: did you think the Mastery-Roll was a good way to balance the powers? Did it affect your Willpower pool in a meaningful way?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prometheus Presence had a little too long range.<br /> Hephaestus' arrows has too long range.<br /> * Aodh's volley has too long range </div> </div> </div>Yep, I got that response pretty often <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> this is going to be fixed in the next version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Too many prerequisites - You have to choose from start to go either fireball lobbiing way or seer way. No other discipline has so many prereqs </div> </div> </div>So I thought about that quite some time. First I only had the prerequisits between the range and close-combat abilities, so you can't mix them and get some kind of invincible firelord. I chose to expand that to the seer-abilities too, but I can see myself removing the prerequisits here, because it doesn't affect combat that much and those are more utility abilities anyway. It will depend on the further responses I get, but right now I think this will be different in the next version. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Promethus' Insight says that &quot;the caster is also more aware of fires and a bit more resistant to falling into R\u00f6tschreck&quot; But this is not supported in the powers description. </div> </div> </div>You are right, there is a sentence missing in the system description. It should be the same as &quot;A Sense For Flames&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I hope you guys had fun playing with the discipline &lt;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26583-comboi","name":"Comboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26583_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}